---
/** Day 052 · Stillwater · Privacy. */
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import Shell from '../../components/day-052/Shell.astro';
const B = '/day-052-yoga-studio';
---
<Site title="Privacy · Stillwater" description="How Stillwater uses the details you give us when you book a class or write to us, how long we keep them and your rights." themeColor="#0c2a31" icon="S" day={52}>
  <Shell>
    <header class="sw-pagehead"><div class="sw-wrap"><ol class="sw-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><li><a href={`${B}/`}>Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Privacy</li></ol><h1 class="sw-h1">Privacy.</h1></div></header>
    <section class="sw-section"><div class="sw-wrap">
      <div class="sw-prose">
<p>This page explains what Stillwater Studio Ltd does with your details. We are at 9 Kensington Gardens, Brighton BN1 4AL. Last updated 24 October 2026.</p>
<h2>What we ask for, and why</h2>
<p>When you book a class we ask for your name and email so we can hold your place, send a confirmation and tell you if a class changes. When you write to us through the contact form we use your name, email and message to reply. If you tell us about an injury or a pregnancy, that note goes to your teacher and nobody else.</p>
<h2>What we do not do</h2>
<p>We do not sell your details, share them for advertising, or send marketing you did not ask for. We do not run advertising or tracking tools on this website.</p>
<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<p>Booking records are kept for twelve months after the class so we can answer questions about a visit or a payment. Messages are kept for twelve months. After that they are deleted.</p>
<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask to see what we hold about you, to correct it or to have it deleted. Email <a href="mailto:hello@stillwateryoga.co.uk">hello@stillwateryoga.co.uk</a> and we will answer within one month. If you are unhappy with how we handled something, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at ico.org.uk.</p>
<h2>On this device</h2>
<p>The timetable remembers the classes you book in your browser's own storage so that “Booked” shows up on every page. See the <a href={`${B}/cookies/`}>cookies page</a> for exactly what is stored.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>
  </Shell>
</Site>
